#### 9. Assertion Roulette
**Test:** `CalculateTotal_ReturnsCorrectAmount` (line 69)
```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount);   // which one failed?
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount);       // no message on any
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal);     // of the three
```
**Risk:** 3 assertions with no descriptive messages. When one fails, the MSTest output shows `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<X>. Actual:<Y>.` — you must open the code to figure out *which* property was wrong.
**Fix:** Add message parameters:
```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount, "Subtotal mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount, "Tax mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal, "Grand total mismatch");
```

